From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RCT Screensaver <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:04:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Screensaver: a generator and plugins shipped in the data
 folder

Plugins in <data folder>/plugin/*.js load with the user's, unless the user
plugin folder holds a file of the same name, which replaces it; overlay images
under the user plugin folder fall back to the shipped plugin folder.

When no generator is registered in <user directory>/screensaver/generator.json,
or the registered one's Python or script is gone, builds and the playlist
dialogs run the generator shipped in <data folder>/screensaver/tools with a
Python shipped beside it (Windows: screensaver/python/python.exe) or else the
first on the PATH (Windows: python.exe outside WindowsApps, python3.exe, then
the py launcher; elsewhere python3, then python).

screensaver.generator ({ available, shipped, python, script, reason }) tells
a plugin whether a generator can run and why not, so it can gray out its
build buttons before a click.
